WEBVTT

00:02.697 --> 00:04.707
Hey, did you hear?

00:04.707 --> 00:07.707
She got hitched to that 
guy she hit it off with.

00:07.707 --> 00:09.727
Y-You don't say!

00:09.727 --> 00:12.027
Lucky her! He was hot.

00:12.027 --> 00:13.467
I know, right?

00:13.467 --> 00:15.747
Have you got a crush on anyone, Nina?

00:15.987 --> 00:18.097
More like, how is it going with Gino?

00:18.097 --> 00:18.927
Gino?!

00:18.927 --> 00:21.487
And then she got all 
flustered all of a sudden.

00:22.167 --> 00:24.847
I've never seen anybody 
make a face like that!

00:22.867 --> 00:25.427
G-Gino and I aren't like that.

00:25.737 --> 00:28.527
Anyway, I'm going to live 
only for the blade.

00:28.527 --> 00:31.487
I guess that's what it takes 
to be the Mad Dog's rival.

00:31.487 --> 00:34.297
You've got no time for romance, huh?

00:44.907 --> 00:47.067
The Mad Dog never changes.

00:47.067 --> 00:49.517
Was she sparring with the 
Sword God, do you think?

00:52.857 --> 00:56.127
I bet you could never get 
yourself a man, anyway!

00:56.427 --> 00:59.867
Have fun living for the sword and staying 
a virgin the rest of your life!

01:03.797 --> 01:06.007
Wh-What?

01:06.007 --> 01:10.507
Sorry to disappoint you, 
but I'm not a virgin!

01:11.667 --> 01:14.117
You're kidding. Who'd you do it with?

01:14.117 --> 01:16.687
Someone I grew up with.

01:16.967 --> 01:19.127
Rudeus is amazing!

01:19.127 --> 01:22.617
We became adventurers and journeyed home 
from the Demon Continent together,

01:22.617 --> 01:25.207
and he even landed a blow on Orsted!

01:25.207 --> 01:28.097
Liar! The Dragon God's 
aura is beyond belief!

01:28.097 --> 01:31.797
My dad said it takes a true master 
to so much as scratch him!

01:31.797 --> 01:33.247
I'm no liar.

01:33.247 --> 01:35.737
Rudeus is a true master.

01:37.637 --> 01:40.427
I'm not a good match for him 
the way I am now.

01:41.197 --> 01:43.357
I've got to get stronger.

01:52.347 --> 01:58.017
<b>III</b>

01:52.347 --> 01:58.017
<b><i>Mushoku Tensei</i></b>

01:52.347 --> 01:58.017
<b><b><i>Jobless Reincarnation</i></b></b>

01:52.627 --> 01:57.047
There's no way "Rudeus" exists 
outside of Eris's imagination.

02:01.937 --> 02:03.237
Rudeus?

02:03.237 --> 02:06.967
Yes! An adventurer. 
I'm guessing you've never heard of him?

02:08.367 --> 02:12.897
Nah, every adventurer 
knows "Quagmire Rudeus."

02:13.617 --> 02:17.097
They say Stepped Leader tried 
to recruit him more than once.

02:17.097 --> 02:20.437
I hear he took down a stray red 
dragon on his own not long ago.

02:20.437 --> 02:21.827
Crazy, right?

02:21.827 --> 02:23.377
He took a red dragon solo?

02:23.377 --> 02:25.077
Now that's something!

02:25.817 --> 02:29.167
Did you find anything on Rudeus, 
the adventurer I asked you to investigate?

02:29.167 --> 02:32.397
Sure. He's famous, 
so it didn't take long.

02:32.397 --> 02:33.727
Y-You're kidding!

02:33.727 --> 02:35.717
Rudeus Greyrat.

02:35.717 --> 02:38.267
Saint-class Water Mage at age five.

02:38.267 --> 02:43.357
When he was seven, he became 
Eris Boreas Greyrat's tutor in Fittoa.

02:43.357 --> 02:45.147
He went missing after that,

02:45.147 --> 02:49.357
but lately he's made a name for himself 
as an adventurer, "Quagmire Rudeus."

02:49.357 --> 02:52.627
The University of Magic invited him 
to be a special student there,

02:52.627 --> 02:54.237
so right now he lives in 
Sharia, the City of...

02:57.337 --> 03:01.837
Rudeus isn't... just some fantasy prince
that Eris dreamed up?

03:03.277 --> 03:03.947
Hang on.

03:04.267 --> 03:08.287
Sure, his record sounds impressive, 
but he's only an adventurer.

03:08.287 --> 03:11.477
Slaying a red dragon single-handed 
sounds like a tall tale,

03:11.477 --> 03:16.247
and with a lame nickname like "Quagmire," 
maybe he's really nothing special.

03:16.897 --> 03:18.087
I know!

03:20.267 --> 03:22.017
Just you wait, Eris!

03:22.017 --> 03:26.557
I'll beat your Rudeus and drag him 
in front of you as my servant!

03:35.997 --> 03:39.897
Mages look a lot brawnier 
than I thought they would.

03:39.897 --> 03:42.327
I can find Rudeus over there, then?!

03:42.327 --> 03:43.577
You have my thanks!

03:43.577 --> 03:45.057
Rudeus.

03:48.887 --> 03:51.077
You seek to duel Rudeus as well?

03:51.077 --> 03:52.657
Y-Yes.

03:56.917 --> 03:59.607
I take it that you, sir, 
are "Quagmire" Rudeus!

03:59.607 --> 04:02.167
I challenge you to a matrimonial duel!

04:07.437 --> 04:08.777
Um...

04:08.777 --> 04:13.377
Is this one of those proposal challenges 
that are in vogue right now?

04:11.437 --> 04:13.217
<i>This is Rudeus.</i>

04:13.377 --> 04:14.307
Indeed!

04:13.687 --> 04:18.827
<i>He's in fairly good shape, but I don't 
sense any kind of aura from him.</i>

04:14.307 --> 04:18.817
I beg your pardon, but I'm straight,

04:18.817 --> 04:20.567
you see, so...

04:18.827 --> 04:20.567
<i>He's not bad-looking.</i>

04:20.867 --> 04:23.497
<i>But there's nothing appealing 
about him as a man.</i>

04:20.937 --> 04:22.667
You have no right to refuse!

04:22.667 --> 04:26.697
I wrote to Lady Pursena, and she informed 
me that you are the boss of her pack!

04:23.497 --> 04:25.327
<i>He's perfect for Eris.</i>

04:25.947 --> 04:28.777
All right. I'll wipe the 
floor with him and—

04:26.697 --> 04:29.577
Thus, you are duty-bound 
to accept all challengers!

04:29.977 --> 04:32.957
Now, have at you!

04:34.777 --> 04:37.367
Well, I'd say that's over.

04:38.987 --> 04:42.377
How could a mage beat a 
fighter at that distance?

04:42.377 --> 04:43.467
Hang on.

04:43.467 --> 04:45.977
That beast man must have 
just been a pushover.

04:47.037 --> 04:50.947
You there. I'm looking for 
a mage called Rudeus.

04:50.947 --> 04:54.167
What? You want to challenge him, too?

04:54.167 --> 04:55.267
Y-Yes.

04:56.987 --> 04:59.897
Then get to the back of the line!

05:05.957 --> 05:09.457
What are you all lined up for? 
Some kind of festival?

05:09.747 --> 05:13.507
We're waiting our turn to 
challenge Rudeus Greyrat!

05:13.507 --> 05:14.847
All of you?!

05:14.847 --> 05:18.317
Could I convince you to let 
me take a crack at him first?

05:18.317 --> 05:21.587
Not unless you beat everyone in line!

05:21.847 --> 05:24.347
A fine idea! I like the sound of that!

05:24.347 --> 05:27.727
Now, all of you come at me at once!

05:27.967 --> 05:31.297
I am the Immortal Demon King Badigadi!

05:31.297 --> 05:35.097
Defeat me, and I shall grant 
you the title of hero!

05:35.337 --> 05:37.127
You don't know who you're messing with!

05:37.127 --> 05:38.957
Get him!

05:38.957 --> 05:39.977
Huh?

05:39.977 --> 05:42.317
You think you're hot shit?!

05:40.587 --> 05:41.607
What?!

05:54.917 --> 05:56.267
Ow, ow, ow...

05:59.607 --> 06:01.627
All right. Get ready.

06:01.627 --> 06:03.757
Indeed I am!

06:17.557 --> 06:20.197
He beat that Demon King in one strike?

06:20.577 --> 06:24.837
Eris is trying to stand on 
equal footing with <i>him?</i>

07:24.157 --> 07:27.087
Thank you for coming all this way.

07:27.337 --> 07:29.977
The trip can't have been 
easy on your old bones,

07:29.977 --> 07:31.467
Water God.

07:31.467 --> 07:33.237
You can say that again.

07:33.237 --> 07:39.477
But a humble request from you is 
so rare that I couldn't stay away.

07:39.997 --> 07:43.727
So, what do you want me 
to teach, and to whom?

07:45.857 --> 07:47.717
By your leave.

07:55.797 --> 07:57.447
Keep calm.

08:08.497 --> 08:09.837
Let me introduce you.

08:10.177 --> 08:14.817
This old lady is the head of the 
Water God Style, Reida Lia.

08:14.817 --> 08:17.517
It's a pleasure to see 
you again, Water God.

08:17.517 --> 08:21.527
Oh, is that you, Nina? How you've grown.

08:21.527 --> 08:23.807
I suppose you're a Sword King by now?

08:23.807 --> 08:26.477
No, I still have much to learn.

08:26.787 --> 08:32.007
I feel confident that I'm the fastest 
here, but I'm not the strongest.

08:32.007 --> 08:34.247
Hey! Sit down!

08:34.247 --> 08:35.607
Where are your manners?!

08:35.607 --> 08:42.077
Eris, this old lady is gonna teach 
you all about the Water God Style.

08:43.037 --> 08:44.587
Nice to meet you.

08:45.007 --> 08:47.307
She's like a wild beast.

08:47.707 --> 08:53.457
Sorry, Gal my boy, but she's not 
cut out for the Water God Style.

08:53.457 --> 08:55.467
I already know that.

08:55.757 --> 08:58.437
Then what do you want me to teach her?

08:58.437 --> 09:00.417
You don't have to teach her anything.

09:00.417 --> 09:02.617
Just be her opponent.

09:05.017 --> 09:09.947
What, are you hoping to have 
that animal assassinate me?

09:09.947 --> 09:11.567
'Course not.

09:11.567 --> 09:15.077
Why kill an old lady who'll drop 
dead on her own any day now?

09:15.507 --> 09:17.677
Tell me, then.

09:17.677 --> 09:21.047
Who are you going to 
send her out to fight?

09:22.417 --> 09:26.917
Eris there says she wants to 
take down Dragon God Orsted.

09:28.587 --> 09:31.957
I'll be. The Dragon God?

09:33.647 --> 09:36.507
That's a lofty goal.

09:36.507 --> 09:38.217
Do you think she can do it?

09:38.567 --> 09:40.857
I think she can.

09:41.137 --> 09:42.717
So does she.

09:43.097 --> 09:45.187
Color me intrigued.

09:45.187 --> 09:50.707
But I won't coddle 
someone with no talent.

09:50.707 --> 09:52.837
You'll face my apprentice first.

09:52.837 --> 09:55.697
If you get good enough to beat 
her handily, you'll train with me.

09:58.077 --> 10:00.207
I've heard of your circumstances.

10:01.237 --> 10:04.697
I am Water King Isolde Cluel.

10:04.697 --> 10:06.507
It's a pleasure to make 
your acquaintance.

10:07.067 --> 10:09.417
I'm Sword Saint Nina Farion.

10:09.417 --> 10:10.687
It's nice to meet you.

10:10.687 --> 10:12.377
Eris Greyrat.

10:14.467 --> 10:18.517
My master told me to spar 
with you, and I will,

10:18.517 --> 10:23.057
but don't imagine mere Saints 
can beat <i>me</i> "handily."

10:25.967 --> 10:29.207
I suppose not. 
I hope you'll be gentle with us.

11:15.537 --> 11:17.277
Whenever you're ready.

11:30.627 --> 11:32.257
I beat her.

11:35.887 --> 11:38.587
Funny how that turned out.

11:38.587 --> 11:41.017
There's nothing funny about it.

11:41.427 --> 11:44.457
Well, I suppose it's a 
fine enough outcome.

11:45.267 --> 11:50.147
What will you do now? 
Study the Water God Style under me?

11:50.147 --> 11:54.197
No, thank you. I still hope to 
master the Sword God Style.

11:54.197 --> 11:57.547
Oh, is that so? I'm glad to hear it.

11:57.547 --> 12:02.227
Well then, why not have the 
three of them spar for a while

12:02.227 --> 12:04.707
and spur each other on?

12:04.707 --> 12:06.457
Might as well.

12:07.007 --> 12:10.407
Right. Train with your masters 
as usual in the mornings,

12:10.407 --> 12:13.087
then train together once 
the sun starts going down.

12:13.087 --> 12:14.117
Yes, sir.

12:14.117 --> 12:15.427
I understand.

12:35.057 --> 12:37.187
It seems I win again.

12:37.707 --> 12:43.457
You beat Eris, I beat you, 
and Eris beats me.

12:43.457 --> 12:45.167
We'll never have a clear winner.

12:46.827 --> 12:49.297
Why don't we talk it over together?

12:49.297 --> 12:51.127
What would be the point?

12:51.127 --> 12:55.697
In the Water God Style, we help each 
other improve by sharing advice.

12:56.877 --> 12:58.757
I wouldn't mind.

13:01.107 --> 13:03.757
Fine. Let's do it.

13:04.467 --> 13:05.827
That's settled, then.

13:05.827 --> 13:07.027
Now...

13:08.167 --> 13:09.887
Come on! I can't hear you!

13:09.127 --> 13:11.967
is there anywhere a little 
quieter we could go?

13:12.347 --> 13:13.737
Let me think...

13:18.567 --> 13:21.077
Now, let me be frank.

13:21.077 --> 13:23.857
Eris, you show too much animosity.

13:24.197 --> 13:27.547
We of the Water God Style 
are sensitive to it,

13:27.547 --> 13:30.927
and we can counter your attacks 
when we know they're coming.

13:30.927 --> 13:34.787
Easy for you to say, but I 
don't know what to do about it.

13:34.787 --> 13:36.407
That's a fair point.

13:37.067 --> 13:41.117
Nina, you show hardly any animosity. 
How do you do it?

13:41.117 --> 13:43.297
I don't know what to tell you.

13:43.297 --> 13:46.137
Moving my sword as fast as 
possible is all it takes to win,

13:46.137 --> 13:48.227
so why would I bother 
trying to menace you?

13:49.527 --> 13:51.107
I don't understand.

13:52.237 --> 13:55.187
How am I not able to beat <i>you?</i>

13:55.187 --> 13:56.607
It's a blow to my self-esteem.

13:57.627 --> 14:01.457
Because I make it so you 
start moving after I do.

14:02.797 --> 14:05.107
Ruijerd taught me how.

14:05.107 --> 14:11.167
I can change where I'm looking and stuff 
so people move before or after I do.

14:11.167 --> 14:13.717
Ruijerd? Who's he?

14:13.717 --> 14:15.447
My teacher.

14:15.857 --> 14:21.517
In other words, you're deliberately 
manipulating your opponent's actions?

14:21.517 --> 14:22.707
That's right.

14:24.507 --> 14:27.147
I see. And do you do this to me as well?

14:27.147 --> 14:30.057
I try, but you don't move.

14:30.057 --> 14:33.017
I've been trained not to.

14:33.937 --> 14:37.777
Why not try holding off on that and 
restraining your animosity next time?

14:38.927 --> 14:40.437
I'll give it a try.

14:41.287 --> 14:43.857
So, what do you think I should do?

14:43.857 --> 14:45.697
That's a good question.

14:46.097 --> 14:49.437
Have you considered asking your master?

14:49.437 --> 14:54.247
If I could get a straight answer from him,
we wouldn't be training together.

14:58.837 --> 15:01.657
What good did talking it over do?

15:04.887 --> 15:05.917
Hey.

15:05.917 --> 15:06.967
What?

15:06.967 --> 15:10.027
Why do you have a coat that 
looks like Ghislaine's?!

15:10.957 --> 15:15.237
Oh, we have them made for us 
when we become Sword Saints.

15:15.237 --> 15:17.717
I don't wear it much because 
it's not my style.

15:18.017 --> 15:19.807
I don't have one!

15:19.807 --> 15:21.987
Go hunt one down yourself 
if you want one that badly.

15:21.987 --> 15:23.817
I doubt it would give you any trouble.

15:25.387 --> 15:26.907
What do you mean, "hunt one down"?

15:26.907 --> 15:30.727
We have to go hunt monsters for 
our test to become Sword Saints.

15:30.727 --> 15:33.507
You make a coat from a pelt 
of a monster you killed,

15:33.507 --> 15:35.697
and that proves you're a Sword Saint.

15:35.697 --> 15:38.097
Where are those monsters?

15:38.097 --> 15:40.677
In the forest west of here, 
where the waterfall is.

15:40.677 --> 15:41.877
It's not that far.

15:42.147 --> 15:43.717
Show me the way.

15:46.107 --> 15:47.457
Pardon me.

15:47.797 --> 15:50.307
May I accompany you?

16:07.787 --> 16:10.657
I'm sure you'll both be fine,

16:10.657 --> 16:14.237
but there are a lot of them, 
and they're fast, so be careful.

16:14.237 --> 16:18.857
I haven't fought monsters much, 
so I'm feeling nervous.

16:18.857 --> 16:21.417
It's easier than parrying 
that animal there.

16:21.417 --> 16:23.707
Hey. Where are the monsters?

16:23.707 --> 16:25.617
They'll come when we build a fire.

16:25.617 --> 16:26.887
Be patient.

16:34.677 --> 16:36.527
Isn't that weird?

16:36.527 --> 16:40.017
Let the great protection of fire 
be on the place thou seekest.

16:40.017 --> 16:43.157
I call the bold heat of 
a torch here and now.

16:43.157 --> 16:44.507
Fireball!

16:48.247 --> 16:50.697
You know magic?

16:50.697 --> 16:52.617
I learned it from Rudeus.

16:52.617 --> 16:54.837
He taught me to read and write, too.

16:54.837 --> 16:57.127
You know magic, reading, <i>and</i> writing?!

16:57.127 --> 16:58.817
So does Ghislaine.

16:58.817 --> 17:02.657
He taught me to speak Demon-God when we 
adventured on the Demon Continent, too,

17:02.657 --> 17:05.637
and he could speak with the 
beast people in the Great Forest.

17:06.177 --> 17:08.627
Rudeus is amazing.

17:12.467 --> 17:13.297
You know—

17:21.567 --> 17:23.407
Those are the monsters.

17:32.747 --> 17:34.157
Wow.

17:35.267 --> 17:38.307
Ugh! She's letting a 
bunch of them through!

18:15.227 --> 18:17.437
I must say, I enjoyed that.

18:17.857 --> 18:21.827
I've never had a chance to train, 
and talk, and go monster hunting

18:21.827 --> 18:26.457
with girls who can wield a sword 
about as well as me before now.

18:26.457 --> 18:28.417
True. Neither have I.

18:33.377 --> 18:35.657
Well then, this is where I leave you.

18:35.657 --> 18:37.847
Thank you for everything today.

18:37.847 --> 18:40.357
I'm glad we talked things over.

18:40.357 --> 18:44.107
I can feel myself improving as well.

18:49.957 --> 18:52.577
Thank you, too, Eris.

18:53.147 --> 18:55.407
I'll get a hit in on you next time.

18:55.887 --> 18:57.587
I'm looking forward to it.

18:58.027 --> 18:59.847
Now, good night.

19:09.417 --> 19:10.667
What?

19:10.667 --> 19:14.347
You wanted to know how to keep your 
animosity from showing, right?

19:14.697 --> 19:16.477
So what?

19:16.477 --> 19:21.437
You should try soaking in a bath, 
getting yourself clean, eating dinner,

19:21.437 --> 19:26.847
and sleeping in a nice, warm bed, 
maybe thinking about that guy you love.

19:26.847 --> 19:28.157
What for?

19:28.157 --> 19:30.237
And what does Rudeus have 
to do with anything?

19:31.937 --> 19:35.917
You seem a whole lot less murderous 
when you're talking about him,

19:35.917 --> 19:37.227
so give it a try.

19:41.097 --> 19:44.417
Anyway, he'll dump you if you 
let yourself get too dirty.

19:52.607 --> 19:57.957
Well, Rudeus was a stickler 
for doing laundry.

20:19.407 --> 20:20.287
Begin!

21:12.087 --> 21:16.147
At the end of the day, 
it appears they're all evenly matched.

21:16.147 --> 21:19.887
But the balance of power 
between them hasn't changed.

21:19.887 --> 21:25.007
Still, they have managed to at 
least win one bout in three.

21:25.007 --> 21:27.887
Yes. They're all improving.

21:27.887 --> 21:30.297
This is what you wanted, 
isn't it, Master?

21:32.457 --> 21:35.957
Well, I guess they are getting better.

21:33.027 --> 21:34.857
You finally did it.

21:34.857 --> 21:36.047
I thought I was going to die.

21:36.047 --> 21:37.907
Holding back is hard.

21:38.207 --> 21:40.107
Next is me and Nina, right?!

21:40.107 --> 21:41.667
That's all for today.

21:41.667 --> 21:42.887
Why?!

21:42.887 --> 21:46.867
We agreed to talk things over 
once we finished sparring.

21:46.867 --> 21:48.377
We did, didn't we?!

21:49.697 --> 21:53.287
Remember to take a bath first!

21:57.137 --> 21:58.557
I know!

22:02.047 --> 22:05.057
Episode 2
Howl, Mad Dog

23:35.057 --> 23:40.137
Next Time
Life Back at Home
